{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1624","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1624","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1624\",\"parent_revision\":\"f6857249228b18c33933677f958213d2d2f756b3c68ad7bd1d9a0c1d881af666\",\"root_revision\":\"f6857249228b18c33933677f958213d2d2f756b3c68ad7bd1d9a0c1d881af666\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`SetActiveTaskConfig` in `sam_schema/core/action_models.py` has no `parent_issue_number` field. The start-task SKILL.md documents agents passing `parent_issue_number` in the config dict for `sam_active_task(action=\\\"set\\\")`, but Pydantic silently drops unknown fields (no `extra='forbid'`). The value is always `None` in the stored `ActiveTaskContext`, breaking the SubagentStop hook's GitHub sub-issue sync.\\n\\nFix: Add `parent_issue_number: int | None = None` to `SetActiveTaskConfig`. Wire it through `server.py` action=\\\"set\\\" case to `ctx_backend.set_active_task(...)`. Add a test verifying the field is stored and retrieved correctly.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `write_task_context()` accepts `parent_issue_number: int | None` parameter\\n- [ ] Context JSON write includes `parent_issue_number` (or omits if None)\\n- [ ] `read_task_context()` retrieves the field correctly from context JSON\\n- [ ] SubagentStop hook's `sync_completion_to_github()` receives parent issue number from context\\n- [ ] Integration test validates write\u2192read\u2192hook flow for `parent_issue_number`\\n- [ ] GitHub sync functional: task completion syncs to GitHub with parent issue relationship intact\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: setactivetaskconfig missing parent_issue_number breaks github sync in subagentstop hook** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality gate follow-up from #1601 \u2014 code review Phase 1 blocking finding B1\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-06\\n- **Related**: #1617 (task status not updated)\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### RT-ICA Snapshot (2026-04-07)\\n\\n**Goal:** Persist `parent_issue_number` through the active-task context file lifecycle so SubagentStop hook can sync task completion to GitHub sub-issues.\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|-----------|--------|----------|\\n| File path in issue (`action_models.py`) | MISSING | File does not exist in `sam_schema/core/`; issue has wrong path |\\n| Relevant code location | AVAILABLE | `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 `write_task_context()` line ~328, `get_parent_issue_number()` line ~381 |\\n| `write_task_context()` missing param | AVAILABLE | Function signature at line 328 has no `parent_issue_number`; line 340 writes only `task_file_path` and `task_id` |\\n| `get_parent_issue_number()` exists | AVAILABLE | Line 381\u2013406 reads from context JSON correctly \u2014 **read path already works** |\\n| Context is plain JSON, not Pydantic | AVAILABLE | No Pydantic model involved \u2014 the \\\"silent drop\\\" description is inaccurate |\\n| Data source for `parent_issue_number` | MISSING | Unknown where value originates when `/start-task` is called |\\n\\n**Decision: BLOCKED** \u2014 data source unknown (where does `parent_issue_number` come from when `/start-task` is called?)\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** Defect \u2014 incomplete implementation at write boundary\\n\\n**5-Whys:**\\n1. Why is GitHub sync failing? \u2192 `parent_issue_number` is `None` in context\\n2. Why is it `None`? \u2192 `write_task_context()` never writes it\\n3. Why doesn't it write it? \u2192 Function signature doesn't accept the parameter\\n4. Why wasn't it added? \u2192 Implementation skipped the write side while adding the read side\\n5. Why is this a boundary issue? \u2192 Task metadata and hook execution are separate; value must flow through context file\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Role | Change needed |\\n|------|------|--------------|\\n| `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` | Producer (write path) | Add `parent_issue_number` param to `write_task_context()`, line ~328 |\\n| `skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` | Test | Extend to test write path with `parent_issue_number` |\\n| `skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_github_sync.py` | Test | Verify sync uses parent issue number from context |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` | Documentation | Verify `parent_issue_number` usage instructions are accurate |\\n\\n**Note:** Issue describes `sam_schema/core/action_models.py` but that file does not exist. The actual write path is in `task_status_hook.py`. If #1601 added a NEW Pydantic-based path via `sam_active_task`, both paths need to be checked.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` (write_task_context ~L328, get_parent_issue_number ~L381)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` (if a new sam_active_task tool was added by #1601)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Small (S)** \u2014 1-2 hours once data source is confirmed: function signature change (5 lines), JSON write addition (1 line), extend existing tests (10 lines).\\n\\n### Open Question (BLOCKS implementation planning)\\n\\nWhere does `parent_issue_number` originate when `/start-task` is called?\\n- Extracted from plan YAML (Plan model field)?\\n- Passed via MCP tool parameter (`sam_claim`, `sam_read`)?\\n- Derived from GitHub issue metadata?\\n- Provided by orchestrator in context?\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5aa609909fa03bc67d9a52ab419c451d0fa17aad0366ddebe5961a680e848a7e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCv48A\"}"}